# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env
data/.robinhood_mcp_tokens.json

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Generated outputs (never commit tip sheets) ──
# Note: output/ itself is a tracked package (emailer, renderer, templates)
# — only the regenerated artifact subdirectories are ignored.
output/tipsheets/
output/candidates/
output/paper_desk/

# ── Logs (all runtime logs; scan_log.json untracked 2026-07-21 —
#    it appended ~47k lines per commit and is regenerated on each run) ──
logs/

# ── Runtime model state (cached in CI; do not commit) ──
data/iv_history/*.json

# ── Chain-quality readings (one row per ticker per scan, several scans a day) ──
data/data_quality_log.json

# ── Sentiment disk cache (NEWS_CACHE_TTL_MIN, regenerated hourly on every scan) ──
data/cache/

# ── OS / IDE ─────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/settings.json
*.swp

# ── Personal trading record & working notes (kept local, never pushed) ──
# The repo is public. These carry trade-level P&L, win rates and internal session
# notes — the project's code is shared, the operator's record is not. They live on
# disk and in the local v0.9-mvp-local tag / feat/entry-timing branch.
VEGA_Trade_Audit_*.md
VEGA_vs_Tastytrade_Benchmark_*.md
VEGA_SESSION_UPDATE_2026-07-09.md
VEGA_Claude_Code_Session_*.md
VEGA_VSCode_Handoff_*.md
VEGA_EntryTiming_AsBuilt_*.md
VEGA_MVP_RUNBOOK.md
VEGA_Project_Review_*.md
VEGA_PAPER_DESK_README.md

# Ledger snapshots taken before a repair. Data, not source — and they carry the same
# contents as logs/, which is already ignored.
backups/ledgers/

# Backups of .env carry every secret .env does. One was created on 2026-08-27 while enabling
# the Robinhood data source and sat untracked-but-not-ignored for a day; this repository is
# PUBLIC, and it has already leaked three credentials (a NewsAPI key and two Gmail app
# passwords). A timestamped copy of a secrets file is still a secrets file.
.env.bak*
*.env.bak*
.env.*.bak

# durable_write's transient files: a per-process temp (".<pid>.tmp") and an O_CREAT|O_EXCL
# lock, both live only for the duration of one write. They appear in `git status` whenever a
# cycle is mid-write, which is most of the trading day.
*.tmp
*.lock

# CREDENTIAL BACKUPS. Same lesson as the .env.bak rules above, learned again on 2026-09-02:
# a session brief instructed backing the live Robinhood OAuth token up to backups/, and
# backups/ is NOT ignored -- backups/scheduled_tasks/ is tracked and public right now. That
# would have staged a live bearer token into a public repo, which is exactly the NewsAPI leak
# a second time, committed by the work that was meant to be cleaning it up.
#
# backups/ledgers/ is already ignored below/above; these cover the credential cases the
# directory rules do not. A token backup belongs OUTSIDE the repository entirely -- these
# patterns are the safety net, not the plan.
backups/secrets/
*.json.bak*
*.bak-*.json
*_tokens.json
*.token.json
